{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Et my covenant of peace.</b> That he need not fear the blood-avengers of Zimri and Kozbi." "<b>Et my covenant of peace.</b> The verse is defective (i.e., missing a word), and it is as though it wrote את בריתי ברית שלום, after the pattern of כסאך אלקים, which is like saying כסאך כסא אלקים, and similarly הארון הברית, which is like הארון ארון הברית, and many more. Another interpretation: <b>my covenant of peace</b> — he was worried lest he lose his priesthood, for they say: a priest who has killed a person shall not lift his hands [to recite the priestly blessing], until the Holy One, blessed be He, assured him: since the act of killing was for the sake of Heaven, as it goes on to explain."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:42.633297904Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}